       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. S0C7DEMO.
       AUTHOR. Z50996.
      *
      *    PURPOSE : DEMONSTRATE S0C7 - DATA EXCEPTION ABEND
      *              ROOT CAUSE: MOVING ALPHABETIC DATA INTO A
      *              PIC 9 FIELD THEN USING IT IN ARITHMETIC
      *
       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.
       SOURCE-COMPUTER. IBM-ZOS.
       OBJECT-COMPUTER. IBM-ZOS.

       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 WS-GROUP.
          05 WS-ALPHA            PIC X(05) VALUE 'HELLO'.
          05 WS-FILLER           PIC X(75) VALUE SPACES.

      *    THIS NUMERIC FIELD OVERLAPS WS-ALPHA IN MEMORY
      *    VIA GROUP LEVEL MOVE - WILL CONTAIN GARBAGE
       01 WS-NUMERIC             PIC 9(05) VALUE ZEROS.
       01 WS-RESULT              PIC 9(05) VALUE ZEROS.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       0000-MAIN.
           DISPLAY '============================================'
           DISPLAY ' S0C7DEMO - DATA EXCEPTION ABEND DEMO      '
           DISPLAY '============================================'
           DISPLAY ' '
           DISPLAY ' EXPLANATION:'
           DISPLAY '  PIC 9 FIELDS USE ZONED DECIMAL FORMAT'
           DISPLAY '  EACH BYTE MUST HAVE HEX F0-F9 (0-9)'
           DISPLAY '  LETTER A = X C1  NOT VALID IN PIC 9'
           DISPLAY ' '
           DISPLAY ' STEP 1: MOVING ALPHA DATA TO NUMERIC...'

      *    MOVE ALPHABETIC DATA INTO NUMERIC FIELD
      *    COBOL ALLOWS THE MOVE BUT THE RESULT IS INVALID
      *    NUMERIC DATA (INVALID ZONE BITS IN EACH BYTE)
           MOVE WS-ALPHA TO WS-NUMERIC

           DISPLAY ' STEP 2: WS-NUMERIC NOW = ' WS-NUMERIC
           DISPLAY '         (LOOKS OK ON DISPLAY BUT IS CORRUPT)'
           DISPLAY ' '
           DISPLAY ' STEP 3: ARITHMETIC WILL NOW CAUSE S0C7...'

      *    *** S0C7 ABEND TRIGGERED HERE ***
      *    ARITHMETIC ON INVALID ZONED DECIMAL = DATA EXCEPTION
           COMPUTE WS-RESULT = WS-NUMERIC * 2

           DISPLAY ' RESULT = ' WS-RESULT
           DISPLAY ' YOU WILL NEVER SEE THIS LINE'
           STOP RUN.
